瓦伦达心态
Wallenda mentality is a mindest that focuses on doing one's own thing without considering the consequences. Its characteristics include being focused, calm, alter, energetic, and performance-oriented. Karl Wallenda, a German-American high-wire performer, was famous for his spectacular and skillful high-wire walks performed without any personal safety measures. However, during a major performance, he tragically lost his balance and died. His wife later revealed that she knew something would go wrong because he kept saying before going on stage that it was too important and must not fail, which was not how he used to think. Previously, he was focused on the act itself and don't worry about the potential outcomes.